.TH BOOTSTRAP.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-commandline-tools 0.2.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
bootstrap.sh \- set up the mu2edaq-commandline-tools venv and CMake build
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./bootstrap.sh
.RB [ \-\-dev ]
.RB [ \-\-cpp ]
.RB [ \-\-clean ]
.RB [ \-\-python
.IR PATH ]
.br
.B ./bootstrap.sh
.BR \-\-version | \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates
.I venv/
in the checkout if it does not exist, upgrades pip, setuptools and wheel, and
installs mu2edaq-commandline-tools into it with
.BR "pip install \-\-editable" ,
so the checkout is what runs.
Safe to re-run; it is also the dependency-refresh command, and
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.sh (1)
calls it on every start unless given
.BR \-\-no\-update .
.PP
Because the install is editable, the Python tools always find the tracked
.I config/mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.yaml
of this checkout on their search path; see
.BR mu2edaq\-tools (1),
section FILES.
.PP
With
.B \-\-cpp
it also configures and builds the CMake targets
.RB ( mu2edaq_cli_core ,
.BR mu2edaq\-tools\-info ,
and the
.B test_cli_core
test driver) under
.I build/
with
.BR CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo .
It does not run
.BR "cmake \-\-install" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dev
Install the
.I dev
extra (pytest) as well.
.TP
.B \-\-cpp
Configure and build the C++ library and tool.
.TP
.B \-\-clean
Remove
.I venv/
and
.I build/
first.
.TP
.BI \-\-python " PATH"
Interpreter used to create the venv.
Default:
.BR $PYTHON ,
else
.BR python3 .
Python 3.9 or newer is required.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print
.B mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools
.I version
(read from
.IR src/mu2edaq_commandline_tools/__init__.py )
and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the script's header comment and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I venv/
The virtual environment.
.TP
.I build/
CMake build tree
.RB ( \-\-cpp ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PYTHON
Default interpreter; overridden by
.BR \-\-python .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
No usable Python 3.9+, no
.B cmake
with
.BR \-\-cpp ,
.B \-\-python
without an argument, or any failing pip or CMake step
.RB ( "set \-e" ).
.TP
.B 2
Unknown option.
.SH EXAMPLES
Development setup with tests and the C++ build:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\&./bootstrap.sh \-\-dev \-\-cpp
source venv/bin/activate
pytest
ctest \-\-test\-dir build \-\-output\-on\-failure
.fi
.RE
.PP
Rebuild from scratch with a specific interpreter:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\&./bootstrap.sh \-\-clean \-\-python /usr/bin/python3.9
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-tools (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-tools\-info (1),
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.sh (1),
.BR stop\-mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.sh (1)
